## Summary

Adds production-oriented forgot/reset password for local-password accounts, integrated with the hardened refresh-session model from #135.

### User flow
- `POST /users/password/forgot` always returns a generic accepted response to avoid account enumeration.
- `POST /users/password/reset` accepts a one-time opaque reset token and a new password.
- Web routes `/forgot-password` and `/reset-password` provide the complete browser flow.

### Security invariants
- raw reset tokens are never persisted; PostgreSQL stores SHA-256 hashes only;
- reset tokens are single-use, expiring and old/parallel tokens are invalidated;
- forgot/reset operations serialize on a pessimistically locked user row before token mutation, preventing concurrent requests from creating multiple active reset credentials;
- reset locks are taken in a consistent `user -> reset token` order;
- password reset increments `users.auth_version`, so already-issued bearer JWTs are rejected immediately instead of remaining usable until access-token expiry;
- all active refresh sessions are revoked on successful reset;
- the reset credential cannot be replayed;
- resetting to the existing password is rejected;
- federated-only/non-password accounts do not receive reset credentials;
- expected invalid/expired-token failures preserve security invalidation state rather than rolling it back.

### Delivery / enumeration resistance
- SMTP delivery occurs asynchronously after the issuing transaction commits;
- API responses do not expose whether an email belongs to an account;
- mail delivery errors are contained outside the HTTP request path;
- production SMTP configuration is explicit and covered by the production Compose contract.

### Runtime / operations
- adds `V51__password_recovery.sql`;
- adds cleanup of expired/consumed reset tokens;
- adds SMTP/password-recovery production settings and deployment documentation;
- adds `.github/scripts/password-recovery-smoke.sh` to the main container runtime gate.

### Validation

Exact branch head `a747b81bce2d900a42bfd16922b05d1a9d3af54e` passed push CI:
- API Maven verify ✅
- Web audit/tests/lint/build ✅
- Production Compose contract ✅
- full Docker/PostgreSQL runtime ✅
- rotating browser auth-session smoke ✅
- password recovery + credential invalidation smoke ✅

The runtime smoke verifies the real reset lifecycle, including invalid/replayed reset tokens, old bearer rejection, old refresh-session rejection and successful authentication with the new password.

## Merge gate

Do not merge unless all PR-triggered workflows are green for this exact latest head SHA, the PR remains mergeable, and the branch is 0 behind `master`. Merge method must be a merge commit with an expected-head guard.
